    <!-- Hero-card split: the metrics column against the vehicle render beside
         it. Weights rather than widths, so the card can be any width and the
         render keeps the same presence. Both fragment_dashboard variants apply
         the pair twice — once to the render row, once to the content row — and
         they have to agree or the metrics run under the car. -->
    <item name="dashboard_hero_body_weight" format="float" type="dimen">60</item>
    <item name="dashboard_hero_art_weight" format="float" type="dimen">40</item>

    <!-- Measurement ceiling for the ribbon backdrop, not a display height.

         The ribbon is a nodpi bitmap, so its intrinsic size is its pixel size
         read as dp — 900 x 400dp. The head unit runs at density 1.0, where that
         is the whole card, and an ImageView showing it at match_parent height
         reports it in the card's first measure pass: the card stretches to 400dp
         and the metrics are left with dead space beneath them.

         ImageView only applies maxHeight when adjustViewBounds is set, and only
         while a dimension is still unresolved. So this caps the first pass, and
         the second pass — where FrameLayout hands match_parent children the
         card's settled height as EXACTLY — ignores it and the ribbon fills the
         card. Any value under the card's ~216dp shortest content height works. -->
    <dimen name="dashboard_hero_backdrop_measure_cap">40dp</dimen>

